From 5b2a858f195c33cec375ce32538c961f5bab3f62 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SWG Local Dev <swg-local@localhost>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 02:19:52 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Sandbox Hoth v1: planet entry, travel point and regions

Hoth (Phase 3) for the test galaxy: terrain and snapshot come from Mod the
Galaxy's archives, the client's planet lists from our local_planets.tre.
planet_manager.lua gets a hoth entry (weather and GCW on, the Scavenger
Starport travel point at 20.3 -1982.2, the landing-pad offset Yavin IV's
outposts use, and a navmesh area over the outpost). hoth_regions.lua adds
the edge no-build strips, the outpost as a city and a no-build zone over
MTG's ice caves. Layout adapted from Bellum Gero's Hoth (AGPL-3.0, pinned
1f4438a1) to MTG's snapshot.

Only loaded where ZonesEnabled lists hoth (test galaxy via test_galaxy.py
--config); live doesn't. Tested: a bot flew Corellia -> Hoth -> Corellia,
21/21 checks (Bot-reports/Esk/20261014-021846-esk-hoth.json).

Agent: Claude
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
